  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool; acc 0.650). The strongest evidence so far is that encoder choice and profile/aggregation settings matter: scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 (+6 pts), multiprofile > singleprofile (+10 pts), and avgpool > transformer (+7 pts with pca). The key untested question is whether scgpt—a pretrained single-cell foundation model—outperforms the VAE-based scvi_n200 representation. config_008 changes only the encoder (scvi_n200 → scgpt) while holding the best-known multiprofile + avgpool settings fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_005. This is the best use of the next budget slot because (1) it directly tests whether a fundamentally different representation paradigm (pretrained generative model vs. VAE) can push performance beyond 0.650, (2) the answer will determine which encoder to pair with image modalities in subsequent multimodal experiments, and (3) unlike re-testing aggregation (config_006), where the prior from pca strongly favors avgpool, the encoder question is genuinely uncertain—pretrained models can either help or hurt depending on task alignment, as the weak resnet50 image result already hints."
}

